{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Pins: saved pane routes, one list per server. A pin's target is a route in the shape protocol/links.json decodes oppi:// links to, without a server, every field of its kind present (null where the link leaves it out). GET /pins answers every pin with what is at its target now where the server checks it (ok, missing, unreadable, workspaceMissing, or unknown when the check took longer than 500 ms): a session, thread, or panel is missing once its session is deleted; a folder or file in the home folder or a workspace's main checkout is probed on disk; a sessions route reads workspaceMissing once its workspace is gone; a game is ok, with its game's name, while the server knows it. Web pages, worktree files, and session-copy files read ok unchecked. POST /pins adds a target (a duplicate answers the saved pin's id; a git or commit route is refused); PUT /pins sets the order and labels and removes left-out pins, and a stale baseRevision answers 409 revision_conflict with the current list. Each change sends the pins_changed app event. Built by server/tests/pins-fixtures.ts; server/tests/pins-fixtures.test.ts fails when the committed bytes differ, and Apple PinsContractTests decodes these bodies.",
    "source": "server/src/types/pins.ts"
  },
